diff --git a/docs/docker-deployment.md b/docs/docker-deployment.md
index 219bcab..6bd5985 100644
--- a/docs/docker-deployment.md
+++ b/docs/docker-deployment.md
@@ -153,6 +153,14 @@ This is for convenience: typically when you self-host you'll be running a single
 
 If you do want to allow multiple accounts to be created in your instance, set `MULTI_TENANT=true`
 
+#### Moving an account from another Fizzy
+
+You can bring an existing account over from another Fizzy instance (fizzy.do, for example) instead of starting from scratch:
+
+1. In the account you want to move, an admin opens **Account settings** and clicks **Export account**. Once the export is ready, they get an email with a download link for a `.zip` file. The link works for a day.
+2. On your instance, sign in with your email address and go to `/account/imports/new` to upload that `.zip` file. Don't complete the signup by creating an account first: in single-account mode, a new account can only be created while there isn't one yet.
+3. You'll get an email when the import is done. The new account has everything from the old one — boards, cards, comments, files and people — and everyone can sign in with the email address they used before.
+
 ## Example
 
 Here's an example of a `docker-compose.yml` that you could use to run Fizzy via `docker compose up`
